APLAN020: a live task waiting on a `dropped` one can never legitimately start.
The plan is deadlocked, and `check`, the gate, must say so rather than pass.

```
$ aplan check
? 1
error[APLAN020] C-002: is `todo` but blocker `C-001` is `dropped`: it can never legitimately start
  --> aplan/tasks/C-002.md:7:1
  fix: Either drop `C-002` too, revive `C-001`, or remove `C-001` from its `blocked_by` and name a real blocker.
failed: 1 error(s), 0 warning(s) across 2 tasks

```

`ready` and `why` already knew: a dropped blocker does not satisfy a dependency.

`ready` also says *which* silence this is. An empty list answers two questions, and
telling them apart is the difference between "the plan is finished or deadlocked"
and "a cut is waiting to be closed" (`A1-105`). Here nothing is closeable, and it
says so rather than printing nothing at all.

```
$ aplan ready
nothing is ready, and no cut is waiting to be closed.

```

```
$ aplan why C-002
C-002 is blocked by:
  C-001 [dropped]  Abandoned approach

```
